=== fix 26 conclusion ===
Repository stays PUBLIC for this PR. The contract Section 15 order is: RC integrated
and approved, deploy access tested, collaborator/Actions/secrets audit done, Owner
approves impact, production no longer depends on anonymous repo access, THEN flip.
Two of those five are false today: the RC is not approved (B1/B2 open, gate not
green on any candidate) and deploy access is not 'tested working' - the last eight
production deploys failed at the migration step (evidence 11). Flipping to private
now would make a broken deploy path harder to see, not safer. The audit above is the
first of the five steps, recorded, not executed; the flip and its retest are Owner
actions after B1 lands. deploy.yml does not read repository visibility, so the flip
itself will not change deploy behaviour, but the deploy must be retested after it
per Section 15 item 2; that retest line is in the M13_REVIEW handover table.

=== clarification on the two 8ae07c5 CI lines above ===
main's tip at snapshot time was d8e3c65 (PR #64). 8ae07c5 is a push to an open
feature branch (ci.yml runs on every push); it is not a mainline deploy and does
not move the frozen candidate. The tip of main is re-checked at 15:55 UTC and is
still d8e3c65. The latest FAILED PRODUCTION deploy run is 35520141104 on d8e3c65
at 15:37 UTC, which extends the failure chain in evidence 11 to nine runs.
