connection failure), for the storefront and for protected paths alike. This sandbox's
egress policy allows npm, GitHub and a few hosts; the production host is not among them.
scripts/verify.sh therefore cannot be executed against the live base from PR7.

What the live security posture IS, from CI-side evidence:
  - deploy.yml runs 'bash scripts/verify.sh' as its last step on every deploy; with
    nine consecutive deploys failing at the step BEFORE verify, live verify results
    since 09:33 UTC do not exist. The last completed live verify is the be1cb99
    deploy recorded in M13 Section 13; it predates PR1/2/4/6/8 code on the host.
  - The contract's rule (Section 13): protected-path evidence is re-run for the frozen
    candidate and never inherited. So fix 25's live 403 proof is PENDING, and the first
    thing it needs is B1 gone (a deploy that reaches the verify step at all).
  - Until then the live host is running 2026-09-20 code against a 2026-09-17-era
    schema (050). Anyone with the host's own shell access should run, read-only:
      bash scripts/verify.sh https://okveggies.com.ng
    and curl -i the five protected paths; append the output here. Owner action.
